<!--
    Fragment: backend-auth  (PASSTHROUGH variant)

    Uploaded as fragment id "map-backend-auth" when identity_mode =
    "passthrough".

    This fragment deliberately does almost nothing, and that is the point.

    In passthrough mode the developer's original Authorization header is
    forwarded to Foundry byte-for-byte. Foundry then performs its OWN Entra
    RBAC check on that same human principal, which is a second, independent
    authorization decision the gateway cannot weaken by misconfiguration.

    Consequence to understand before choosing this mode: because the human
    holds inference RBAC on the Foundry resource, a human who can reach the
    Foundry endpoint can call it directly and skip every gateway control.
    Preventing that requires network controls (the private profile), and
    network controls are only as strong as the rules nobody has edited.

    See docs/architecture.md for the full comparison.
-->
<fragment>
    <!--
        No credential policy here, by design. Adding
        authentication-managed-identity, authentication-basic, or
        authentication-certificate would replace the caller's identity and
        silently convert this deployment into brokered mode without any of
        the RBAC changes that mode requires.

        tests/contract/test_policy_invariants.py enforces that.
    -->
    <set-variable name="identity-mode" value="passthrough" />
</fragment>
